1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,440
ChatGPT has started signing what
it writes in Europe… and you

2
00:00:04,440 --> 00:00:06,490
will never see the signature.

3
00:00:06,650 --> 00:00:08,920
Writing is full of tiny choices.

4
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:10,210
Big or large?

5
00:00:10,210 --> 00:00:11,740
Start or begin?

6
00:00:11,740 --> 00:00:12,920
Either one works.

7
00:00:12,920 --> 00:00:17,000
Now imagine a secret coin makes
every one of those choices.

8
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,560
Only the company knows how it's loaded.

9
00:00:19,570 --> 00:00:21,500
One word proves nothing.

10
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:24,490
But hundreds of words
that all follow the coin?

11
00:00:24,550 --> 00:00:25,950
That's a signature.

12
00:00:25,950 --> 00:00:27,330
No hidden characters.

13
00:00:27,330 --> 00:00:31,100
Copy, paste, even a screenshot…
it's built to survive,

14
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:33,480
because the signature is the words.

15
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:37,260
A new EU law says AI
text must carry a mark.

16
00:00:37,260 --> 00:00:39,970
So in Paris, ChatGPT signs.

17
00:00:39,970 --> 00:00:41,900
In London… not yet.

18
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:45,840
But Claude, another chatbot, now
signs its writing everywhere.

19
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:47,220
The UK included.

20
00:00:47,220 --> 00:00:48,720
So does it work?

21
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:52,960
In OpenAI's own test, it caught
about seven in ten Spanish answers…

22
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:55,060
and fewer than half in Romanian.

23
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:56,320
Here's the twist.

24
00:00:56,320 --> 00:00:59,490
Claude also signs text it only translated.

25
00:00:59,490 --> 00:01:02,160
So your own words can carry its signature.

26
00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:06,190
Anthropic says it plainly: a
mark is a signal, not proof.

27
00:01:06,190 --> 00:01:08,920
And teachers can't use ChatGPT's checker.

28
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:11,500
OpenAI rules out checking student work.

29
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:13,930
So a signature doesn't prove you cheated.

30
00:01:13,930 --> 00:01:16,730
And no signature doesn't
prove a human wrote it.

31
00:01:16,730 --> 00:01:19,670
If AI helped you write
something… just say so.

32
00:01:19,670 --> 00:01:21,720
The words might already be saying it.

33
00:01:21,720 --> 00:01:24,590
Follow for more AI, explained like this.
